<title>RUSSIA: Russia to import 4-5 million tonnes grain in 1997.</title>
<headline>Russia to import 4-5 million tonnes grain in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Agriculture Minister Viktor Khlystun told a news conference on Tuesday that Russia would import 4-5 million tonnes of grain over 1997 from unnamed sources, but said the state would conduct no buying.</p>
<p>&quot;We will import four to five million tonnes of grain over this period for the Far East and the north but the buying will be done by the private sector,&quot; he said. He also said Russia would export 6-7 million tonnes of grain from its 1996 crop.</p>
</text>
